From 56a824a5a5f5dbfd4a1ad259d59dfb332997c21b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 20:48:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] update-check: Reaper GitHub-hosted firmware notification
 (Phase 1, opt-in, notify-only)

Replaces Merlin's fwupdate.asuswrt-merlin.net update check with Reaper's own
GitHub-hosted manifest, so the firmware page and a new dashboard badge report
actual Reaper releases instead of (broken) Merlin version math and Merlin links.

Why the stock check was broken for Reaper: every Reaper release shares the same
Merlin base (3006.102.8); our version lives only in EXTENDNO (Reaper_v2.1.5),
which the stock numeric compare cannot parse and in fact zeroed - so it could
never detect a Reaper update and pointed users at asuswrt-merlin.net.

- rom/webs_scripts/reaper_webs_update.sh: busybox-sh check. Reads productid +
  detects variant (MCP ships rmcpd/Reaper_Advisor.asp, noMCP neither - the same
  signal reaper_verify uses), fetches updates/manifest_3006.txt from the AM-Reaper
  raw tree, greps PRODUCTID#VARIANT, compares Reaper X.Y.Z (padded integer), and
  sets the stock webs_state_* nvram the firmware page already renders. NEVER
  downloads or flashes (Phase 1). Guarantees no cross-variant flash offer.
- rom/webs_scripts/reaper_webs_note.sh: fetches updates/notes/Reaper_v<ver>.txt,
  falls back to a GitHub-releases pointer.
- rom/Makefile: install the reaper_ scripts over webs_update.sh/webs_note.sh
  (was merlin_).
- Advanced_FirmwareUpgrade_Content.asp: download links -> AM-Reaper releases page;
  fw_note3 text de-Merlined.
- Main_ReaperDash.asp: crimson 'New firmware available' badge in the topbar,
  server-rendered from webs_state_flag (zero cost when no update / check off),
  links to the firmware page. Reuses existing dict token FW_new_firmware_available
  (no dict change).

Opt-in preserved: firmware_check_enable default stays 0 (no de-cloud posture
change); the scheduled/background check only runs when the user enables it. The
manual 'Check' button still works on demand. Phase 2 (in-GUI download+flash from
webs_state_url + a native Reaper firmware page) remains backlogged.

NOT BUILT - rides a future rung; METAL OWED (see commit for test plan).
